; MM-EXEC-6b: a `match` on a DIRECT CALL loses tail position when the
; payload is a reference.
;
; THIS PROGRAM IS EXPECTED TO CRASH, and `scripts/check-tail-position.sh`
; requires that it does. It is a defect's own demonstration, pinned so
; that fixing the defect turns the gate red and forces whoever fixes it
; to say so - which is this repository's rule for a quoted-broken
; program everywhere else.
;
; `run` is written in tail position: the recursive call is the whole of
; the `Some` arm. `codegen.ax:12547` routes a match whose scrutinee is a
; direct call to a pair-returning function through `emitMatch` rather
; than `emitMatchTail` when the payload is a reference, so the frame is
; not reused and the stack grows once per iteration.
;
; ITS TWO CONTROLS ARE BESIDE IT AND MUST STAY GREEN. `boxed.ax` binds
; the scrutinee with `let` first; `intpay.ax` carries an `Int` payload
; instead of a `String`. Either change alone makes the same program
; iterate in constant stack, which is what localises the defect to the
; INTERSECTION rather than to recursion depth. Two controls that pass
; are what stop this file from being a test that a deep recursion
; overflows, which would prove nothing.
;
; MEASURED at 2,000,000 iterations on the default stack, exit 139 at
; both `--opt 0` and `--opt 2`. The gate runs it at 20,000 under
; `ulimit -s 512`, where it still fails and both controls still pass -
; milliseconds instead of seconds, which is why this is gateable at all.
(import Str)

(import IO)

(:: step (-> Int (Option String)))

(fn (step n)
  (if (== n 0)
    None
    (Some "x")
  )
)

(:: run (-> Int Int Int))

(fn (run n acc)
  (match (step n)
    ((Some s) (run (- n 1) (+ acc (strLen s))))
    ((None) acc)
  )
)

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  {
    (let ((v (run 20000 0)))
      (println "{v}")
    )
    0
  }
)
